  "description": "The first term of the validation guard, app/cbl/COMEN01C.cbl:127 - WS-OPTION IS NOT NUMERIC - reached with the non-digit OPTIONI '1x'. This is the term that only exists because line 124's MOVE WS-OPTION-X TO WS-OPTION crosses PIC X(02) to PIC 9(02) at equal widths, so the 'x' survives into the numeric field for the class test to detect; a translation that parsed the field into an integer and threw would have replaced a branch the program has with one it does not. Line 125 echoes the unnormalised two characters straight back to OPTIONO. WS-OPTION then denotes no value at all, so the ungated filter at 136-137 has no usable subscript, is false without reading the table, and cannot throw.",
